    {
      "id": "claim_851e8d4871ac4b7eba317b0f2d06fcb6",
      "statement": "ExecutionEngine.recoverInterruptedTasks() is startup-only reconciliation that never replays work, kills unknown PIDs, or clears recovery holds automatically: it fails only confirmed in-process mock executions (metadata execution_recovery_attempt stamp correlated with the latest engine-authored 'admitted' execution_event, executorKind mock, inProcess true, sandboxed false) and pauses everything else with execution_recovery_hold: true and outcome 'unknown', requiring operator reconciliation before redispatch (executeTask rejects held tasks with EXECUTION_RECOVERY_REQUIRED and reserved provenance keys are stripped from user metadata writes so the hold cannot be forged).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/server/src/__tests__/task-recovery.test.ts#L37-L120",
