      "id": "claim_fd9346f3a2dd44f18d65536ed602d2aa",
      "statement": "createRoutes builds the /api router from a declarative mount table where registration order matters: it requires auth service and middleware (throws AUTH_MIDDLEWARE_REQUIRED otherwise), limits bodies to 1 MB with a 300 req/min rate limit, mounts /swarms/spawns (accepting scoped X-Spawn-Token for runtime children) before the generic /swarms requireAuth mount, mounts self-authenticating diff routes at '/' without a mount-level guard so they don't intercept the Telegram webhook, and generates a cached authenticated openapi.json from the same table.",
