    {
      "id": "claim_c9e61527b575480a93d449c51368b7bc",
      "statement": "On SIGTERM the entrypoint stops the ExplainerFleetWorker, gracefully closes every upgraded WebSocket client with code 1001 ('Server shutting down') so httpServer.close() is not blocked, terminates surviving sockets after a 5-second unref'd deadline, closes the WebSocket server, clears the Dennis queue timer, calls telegramGateway.stopAll() to release leases, and then closes the HTTP server, clears the deadline, closes the database, and exits 0. This entrypoint installs no SIGINT handler and does not use the standalone LifecycleManager's signal wiring.",
